            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-center">
                <!-- Textual Content & Etymology Breakdown -->
                <div class="space-y-4">
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-clay font-serif">The Etymology of Lihay-Galad</h3>
                    <p class="text-bark/90 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
                        The title <strong class="text-forest">&quot;Lihay-Galad&quot;</strong> was chosen because it sounds ancient, rhythmic, and deeply rooted in classic Tagalog lore. By combining two ancient root words, it forms a poetic descriptor of my appetite for outdoor adventure:
                    </p>

                    <div class="space-y-3 pt-2">
                        <div class="p-4 bg-parchment rounded-xl border-l-4 border-clay shadow-sm">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-forest text-sm uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center justify-between">
                                <span>1. Lihay (ᜎᜒᜑᜌ᜔)</span>
                                <span class="text-xs text-clay font-normal italic">Root Verb</span>
                            </h4>
                            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-bark/80 mt-1">
                                Means to veer off the beaten path, turn away from the mainstream road, or venture deliberately into the untamed wild.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="p-4 bg-parchment rounded-xl border-l-4 border-forest shadow-sm">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-forest text-sm uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center justify-between">
                                <span>2. Galad (ᜄᜎᜇ᜔)</span>
                                <span class="text-xs text-clay font-normal italic">Archaic Noun/Verb</span>
                            </h4>
                            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-bark/80 mt-1">
                                An archaic root associated with wandering, roaming freely, or traversing vast, untouched lands and thick mountain forests.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <p class="text-sm text-bark/90 italic pt-2">
                        &quot;Joined together, Lihay-Galad translates roughly to &lsquo;The One Who Strays into the Wilderness&rsquo; &mdash; a title I wear with pride on every summit.&quot;
                    </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Unordered List Requirement: Favorites -->
