                    <li class="relative pl-6 sm:pl-8 group">
                        <span class="absolute -left-[17px] top-1.5 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-forest text-parchment font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-parchment shadow">1</span>
                        <div class="bg-parchment p-4 rounded-xl border border-ochre/30 shadow-sm">
                            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-forest">Ang Luntiang Lupain sa Paanan</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-clay font-medium">"Where My Roots Took Hold"</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-bark/80 mt-1, text-justify">Every great mountain journey begins at the base, and mine started surrounded by the lush landscapes and quiet fields of San Miguel, Bulacan. Growing up in the countryside built a strong foundation within me—one rooted in humility, simplicity, and a deep appreciation for nature. These peaceful foothills laid the groundwork for the endurance and character I carry with me today.</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>

                    <li class="relative pl-6 sm:pl-8 group">
                        <span class="absolute -left-[17px] top-1.5 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-clay text-parchment font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-parchment shadow">2</span>
                        <div class="bg-parchment p-4 rounded-xl border border-ochre/30 shadow-sm">
                            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-forest">Ang Paglalakbay</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-clay font-medium">"Stepping Out of My Comfort Zone"</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-bark/80 mt-1, text-justify">Equipped with a backpack full of dreams and determination, I set out on my first major traverse—leaving the familiar paths of my home province to head toward the vast cityscape of Manila. As a young dreamer willing to adapt to new terrain, I embraced the challenge of moving to the metropolis to pursue higher ground and bigger opportunities.</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>

                    <li class="relative pl-6 sm:pl-8 group">
                        <span class="absolute -left-[17px] top-1.5 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-ochre text-bark font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-parchment shadow">3</span>
                        <div class="bg-parchment p-4 rounded-xl border border-ochre/30 shadow-sm">
                            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-forest">Paghakbang</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-clay font-medium">"The Gateway to My Climb"</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-bark/80 mt-1, text-justify">Passing the admissions for the Polytechnic University of the Philippines (PUP) marked my official jump-off point. Standing at the threshold of this institution was proof of my grit and perseverance. This is where my formal climb began—where late nights, lessons, and relentless effort became the essential gear for my upward journey.</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>

                    <li class="relative pl-6 sm:pl-8 group">
                        <span class="absolute -left-[17px] top-1.5 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-moss text-parchment font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-parchment shadow">4</span>
                        <div class="bg-parchment p-4 rounded-xl border border-ochre/30 shadow-sm">
                            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-forest">Matarik na landas</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-clay font-medium">"Navigating the Steepest Slopes"</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-bark/80 mt-1, text-justify">I am currently navigating the high ridge as a 3rd-year university student—balancing demanding academic challenges while continuing to press forward. Amidst the steep climb of student life, I discovered my true sanctuary: the physical trails of mountain hiking.
Each summit I reach in the wild serves as a living reminder of my path: no matter how steep or exhausting the trail of life gets, the view from the top makes every single step worth it.</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>

                </ol>
            </div>
        </section>

